statement:
Let P, n, Q ∈ ℕ, let F be a set of functions ℝ^P → ℝ^Q, and let sing map functions to subsets of ℝ^P. Write φ_{y,λ}(x) := φ(y + λx), and φ_k ⇀ φ for convergence of ∫ f·φ_k dμH[n] to ∫ f·φ dμH[n] for every continuous compactly supported f. Assume:
(A.1) φ_{y,λ} ∈ F for φ ∈ F, 0 < λ < 1, |y| ≤ 1 − λ;
(A.2) for φ ∈ F, |y| < 1 and every strictly decreasing λ_k > 0 with λ_k → 0, there are a strictly increasing sequence of indices sub and ψ ∈ F with φ_{y,λ_{sub(k)}} ⇀ ψ and ψ(λx) = ψ(x) for all λ > 0 and x;
(A.3c) sing φ is closed for φ ∈ F;
(A.3(2)) sing φ_{y,λ} = {x : y + λx ∈ sing φ} for φ ∈ F, 0 < λ < 1, |y| ≤ 1 − λ;
(A.3(3)) if φ, φ_k ∈ F and φ_k ⇀ φ, then for each ε > 0 there is k₀ with B_1(0) ∩ sing φ_k ⊆ {x : ∃ z ∈ sing φ, |x − z| < ε} for all k ≥ k₀.
Let ℓ > 0 and φ ∈ F. Then the set of x ∈ sing φ ∩ B_1(0) for which the following fails is μH[ℓ]-null: there are λ_k (k ∈ ℕ) and ψ with 0 < λ_k < 1 and |x| ≤ 1 − λ_k for all k, λ_k → 0, ψ ∈ F, φ_{x,λ_k} ⇀ ψ, ψ(λz) = ψ(z) for all λ > 0 and z, and μH[ℓ](sing ψ ∩ B_1(0)) > 0.
